          "CONFLICT (p.129-140 sheet titles vs p.128 table): the bracing connection drawn on the sheet \u0027U(n) and U(n)\u0027 details\u0027 fits the table points U(12-n) / U(12-n)\u0027 (drawn gusset angles within 0.4 deg; at U(n) they are geometrically impossible, e.g. sheet U1: 24.6 deg vs \u003E= 36.2 deg at U1). Each sheet is modeled at U(12-n) / U(12-n)\u0027; U6 is its own mirror.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.102, 107, 119, 124): arch pedestal / bearing elevations (B1-B3) - the plan pedestal tops do not reconcile with the WP elevations \u002B bearing stack (0.13-0.20 ft; EL A vs E 0.053 ft). Bearings are built up from the plan pedestal tops; the chain difference is a CHECK row.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.102): which arch pedestal is EL A / EL E - the view direction of the pier elevation is not stated on the sheet. EL A = south at Pier 10 / north at Pier 11, as derived from p.102 \u002B p.91 by the approach model.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.94, 102, 119): CL1 / CL2 relative to the piers (U3) - no combination of the layout offsets reproduces the plan chord 200\u0027-11 11/16. CL1/CL2 = 7\u0022 along the pier \u002B 4 13/16\u0022 toward the span; the local geometry is kept and the difference reported.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.119-150): camber / no-load geometry (U4) - not given. Final geometry modeled.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.152, 143): tie girder web shear studs - the typical arch deck section (p.152) shows a horizontal 7/8\u0022 x 7\u0022 stud on the inside face of each tie web and the tie quantity (p.143 note 1) includes shear studs, but no spacing / count is given on any sheet. Not modeled (the tie quantity check is short by them).",
          "CONFLICT (p.147 vs p.148, p.120): the p.147 table labels H(n) \u0027arch rib working point\u0027 and HC(n) \u0027arch rib cable anchor point\u0027, but HC(n) lies on the rib working line (R 126\u0027-0 through the RS points, within 0.0004\u0027) and H(n) lies 10\u0022 inside it on the cable axis, P1 off the arch plane - exactly the p.148 fin plate pin (P2 sin B = 10\u0022, P1). Modeled: rib pin = H(n), strand and sockets pin to pin; the p.147 cable length (TC to HC) is checked to HC(n) (U6 resolved for the hangers).",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.107, 93): sole plate weld target (U8) - the bearing note and the erection sequence name different plates. Not modeled (welds).",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.119, 124): WP position in the tie / steel underside at the bearings (U10) - the WP is at the bottom of the tie flange (p.119) but drawn inside the 2\u0022 end flange (p.124) and the plate below it is not dimensioned. End flange from 1 1/8\u0022 below to 7/8\u0022 above the WP (tie flange \u002B 1 1/8\u0022 fill = 2\u0022), steel underside 1\u0022 lower.",
          "UNRESOLVED (p.148): hanger sockets vs the supplied WireCo catalog - the plan sockets (pin 1.378\u0022, W 16.18\u0022 / 34.41\u0022) are not the catalog\u0027s 1\u0022 open strand socket (Table 6 p.20: pin 2 1/4\u0022, A 12\u0022). Sockets modeled at the plan table dimensions; the catalog row is reported by check-arch-nht.csx."
        ]
      },
